  "result": {
    "summary": "I ran test_context_eval, test_evidence and test_spawn at head 5fb0694. context_eval no longer fails. The earlier 0.144 vs 0.4 reduction failure was fixed by the 'preserve routing baseline' commit, which no longer lets stable evidence ids collapse the baseline occurrences. The two named acceptance tests are present as unittest methods. Two other test_spawn.Render tests error when run in the batch, and the one I re-ran alone fails with 'Not a valid object name goal/G'. That looks like test-order dependence in the fixture's git setup, not this diff. I did not run the full tests-green.sh gate, so criterion 3 is unconfirmed. The diff adds no new trust-boundary or privilege change. Persisted rows are still redacted, and bus content is treated as data.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/evidence.py",
        "line": 170,
        "issue": "EvidencePool.__init__ and add() now rewrite the whole jsonl with write_text, which is not atomic. Another process appending to the same goal pool at the same time could lose rows or leave a truncated file. Consider a temp-file rename, or accept the risk since the pool is single-writer in practice.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/spawn.py",
        "line": 782,
        "issue": "The routed evidence cap pops items from the end. That can drop the highest-priority items if the router does not sort them by priority, and the cap is applied after the router has already accounted for those tokens in its telemetry. Check that the ordering is priority-first.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "tests/test_spawn.py",
        "line": 799,
        "issue": "test_packet_prior_worker_section_lists_partial_facts and test_prior_worker_section_inert_in_shadow_mode error with 'Not a valid object name goal/G' when run in a batch or alone. They depend on git state created by other tests, so they are order-dependent and may hide real gate results.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
